class LockedDropout(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, p):
        super().__init__()
        self.p = float(p)
    def forward(self, x):
        if not self.training or self.p == 0:
            return x
        keep = 1.0 - self.p
        mask = x.new_empty(x.size(0), 1, x.size(2)).bernoulli_(keep).div_(keep)
        return x * mask

Route forward and encode through one log2feats implementation: item_emb -> locked input dropout -> GRU -> locked output dropout. Each mask is shared across time within a sequence. Preserve the final-nonpadding gather. Save input_dropout and output_dropout in category metadata, extend the model constructor, and update the predictor writer to instantiate that exact architecture before loading its checkpoint. In eval mode both dropout operations are identity functions."
